====Usage notes====
* Often used interchangeably in compounds with {{m|ja|器|tr=ki}} to indicate “machine”, with the distinction that {{lang|ja|機}} implies a larger machine, such as an airplane, while {{lang|ja|器}} implies a smaller device, possibly hand-held. Compare {{m|ja|飛行機|tr=hikōki||airplane}} with {{m|ja|検知器|tr=kenchiki||sensor, detector}}.

====Alternative forms====
[[File:Vending machines in Nakano Broadway.jpg|thumb|right|250px|[[Image:RYAKUJI_ki_01.png|20px]], {{w|ryakuji}} for {{lang|ja|機}}.]]
{{lang|ja|機}} has many {{w|ryakuji}} (handwritten abbreviations), as it is a common character with many strokes (16):
* [[Image:RYAKUJI_ki_01.png|40px]] A {{w|phono-semantic}} simplification from [[on'yomi]] of “ki” (katakana キ): 木 + キ (semantic plus simplified phonetic) – compare [[File:Ryakuji GI.png|30px]] for {{m|ja|議}} and [[File:RYAKUJI ma.png|30px]] for {{m|ja|魔}}/{{m|ja|摩}}. Note that [[キ]] is itself a Heian-period simplification of {{m|ja|幾}}.
* [[Image:RYAKUJI_ki_02.png|40px]] Graphical simplification.
* [[Image:RYAKUJI_ki_03.png|40px]] Graphical simplification.
* [[Image:RYAKUJI_ki_04.png|40px]] Graphical simplification.

